Component exceptions and provenance
-----------------------------------

1. kernel/patches/0001-playbook-winchester-7.3.3.patch,
   kernel/winchester-7.3.3.config,
   kernel/patches/0001-playbook-winchester-6.15.11.patch,
   kernel/patches/winchester.config,
   kernel/clean-kernel-6.15.11-changes.patch (historical) and the files under
   kernel/source/ are derived from Linux 7.3.3 / 6.15.11 and remain licensed
   under GPL-2.0-only.  They are aggregated with, not relicensed by, the
   GPL-3.0-or-later project code.

2. tools/bbusb.py is a Python port of bb10mt's bbusb.pas and ucrypto.pas
   (including the 560-byte QNXH signature constant).  bb10mt is GPL-3.0, so
   this file is a GPL-3.0 derivative and is distributed here under
   GPL-3.0-or-later.  The bb10mt source itself is NOT included in this
   repository.

3. tools/pre_os_ifs_flash.py reads the `signature_data` constant from a
   user-supplied bb10mt checkout (`qcfm.pas`).  The bb10mt source is not
   included; users must obtain it themselves, or use `tools/bbusb.py flash`,
   which carries the constant.

4. tools/BerryShell-V4.py is derived from the author's own earlier
   BerryShell-V3.py, not from a third-party project.  Its qconn protocol layer
   was reverse-engineered by the author.

5. The protocol and format facts, register values, disassembly notes and
   measurements in docs/ are the project's own analysis.  They may reference
   proprietary systems, but no proprietary binary, datasheet, TRM or device
   image is included.

Not included in this repository
-------------------------------

The proprietary QNX/BlackBerry binaries and device dumps, the TI OMAP4430 TRM
and TWL6030 datasheet, the Toshiba TC358764 datasheet, the BlackBerry vendor
images (IFS/RCFS/UFS), the sealed IFS, the SSH keys, the ramloader blobs and the
bb10mt source are deliberately excluded.  See `docs/project/DECISIONS.md` and
`.gitignore` for the current policy.

